  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math>&nbsp;positive consecutive terms&nbsp;of an arithmetic progression. If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math> is its common difference, then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo></mrow></munder><msqrt><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></math>",
